          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-legislation-amendment-act-2011-sch-2-sec-21-ss-3-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-legislation-amendment-act-2011-sch-2-sec-21-ss-3-logic-epistemic-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "328bd36575e72e53604e4df3d22cf7506d516fc767e3411a245e768e3e44573a",
      "skos:note": "Court must not consider unforeseeable circumstances when determining contravention."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-legislation-amendment-act-2011#sch-2-sec-21-ss-3",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "21(3) Unconscionable conduct in connection with goods or services",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 14,
      "values:originalText": "(3) For the purpose of determining whether a person has contravened\nsubsection (1):\n\n(a) the court must not have regard to any circumstances that\nwere not reasonably foreseeable at the time of the alleged\ncontravention; and\n\n(b) the court may have regard to conduct engaged in, or\ncircumstances existing, before the commencement of this\nsection."
    },
