    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-legislation-amendment-act-2011-sch-2-sec-21-ss-4",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "21(4) Unconscionable conduct in connection with goods or services",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-legislation-amendment-act-2011#sch-2-sec-21-ss-4"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-legislation-amendment-act-2011.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-legislation-amendment-act-2011.pdf, p.14",
      "values:originalText": "(4) It is the intention of the Parliament that:\n\n(a) this section is not limited by the unwritten law relating to\nunconscionable conduct; and\n\n(b) this section is capable of applying to a system of conduct or\npattern of behaviour, whether or not a particular individual is\nidentified as having been disadvantaged by the conduct or\nbehaviour; and\n\n(c) in considering whether conduct to which a contract relates is\nunconscionable, a court’s consideration of the contract may\ninclude consideration of:\n\n(i) the terms of the contract; and\n\n(ii) the manner in which and the extent to which the\ncontract is carried out;\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2011A00184\n\nUnconscionable conduct  Schedule 2\n\nand is not limited to consideration of the circumstances\nrelating to formation of the contract.",
      "skos:definition": "(4) It is the intention of the Parliament that:\n\n(a) this section is not limited by the unwritten law relating to\nunconscionable conduct; and\n\n(b) this section is capable of applying to a system of conduct or\npattern of behaviour, whether or not a particular individual is\nidentified as having been disadvantaged by the conduct or\nbehaviour; and\n\n(c) in considering whether conduct to which a contract relates is\nunconscionable, a court’s consideration of the contract may\ninclude consideration of:\n\n(i) the terms of the contract; and\n\n(ii) the manner in which and the extent to which the\ncontract is carried out;\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2011A00184\n\nUnconscionable conduct  Schedule 2\n\nand is not limited to consideration of the circumstances\nrelating to formation of the contract.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-legislation-amendment-act-2011-sch-2-sec-21"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-legislation-amendment-act-2011-sch-2-sec-21-ss-4-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-legislation-amendment-act-2011-sch-2-sec-21-ss-4-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "6b25b2dbc88df070556eda032a2f8d2cd85a68437050ff650af6ae8b2943a4bc",
      "skos:note": "Court must consider contract terms and manner of performance when determining unconscionable conduct."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-legislation-amendment-act-2011#sch-2-sec-21-ss-4",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "21(4) Unconscionable conduct in connection with goods or services",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 14,
      "values:originalText": "(4) It is the intention of the Parliament that:\n\n(a) this section is not limited by the unwritten law relating to\nunconscionable conduct; and\n\n(b) this section is capable of applying to a system of conduct or\npattern of behaviour, whether or not a particular individual is\nidentified as having been disadvantaged by the conduct or\nbehaviour; and\n\n(c) in considering whether conduct to which a contract relates is\nunconscionable, a court’s consideration of the contract may\ninclude consideration of:\n\n(i) the terms of the contract; and\n\n(ii) the manner in which and the extent to which the\ncontract is carried out;\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2011A00184\n\nUnconscionable conduct  Schedule 2\n\nand is not limited to consideration of the circumstances\nrelating to formation of the contract."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-legislation-amendment-act-2011-sch-2-sec-21-ss-4-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-legislation-amendment-act-2011-sch-2-sec-21-ss-4"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
